WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.950
Have you lived around here for long?

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.950
All my life.

3
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.950
Did your parents live in this house too?

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.950
And my grandparents.

5
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.950
Right behind it is the house
where Mihail Sadoveanu lived.

6
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.950
Which is in ruins now, sadly.

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.950
It caught fire about 15 years ago.

8
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:31.950
The elderly lady, the last
member of the Sadoveanu family,

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.950
made an agreement with someone to care for her
until her death, in exchange for the house.

10
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.950
About six months after she was moved
to her new place, she passed away.

11
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:53.950
Nobody lived in the house after
that; homeless people moved in.

12
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:02.950
And about fifteen years ago, just
before Christmas, it caught fire.

13
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.674
It was a huge commotion at the time.

14
00:01:06.724 --> 00:01:08.950
The fire brigade came.

15
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.950
It lost its roof, and it's
been falling apart ever since.

16
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.950
Sadly. What can you do?

17
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.796
I don't have time for nostalgia.

18
00:01:17.846 --> 00:01:18.950
– You don't, do you?

19
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:25.157
No, it's just that this used to be a very
quiet neighbourhood, but as the area's

20
00:01:25.207 --> 00:01:27.950
developed, it's filled up with cars.

21
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:34.950
If you come at eight in the morning, when the
kids are going into school, you can't get through

22
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.950
for all the cars.

23
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:42.950
There are two schools of thought: one that holds
on to history, one that's all about modernism.

24
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.950
Around here you'll see a number of
houses built in a particular style.

25
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:55.620
Go a bit further on and you'll see boxy
blocks of flats that have no business being

26
00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:57.950
in a neighbourhood like this.

27
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:03.950
That's my view. Others come along
and say we need to modernise.

28
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.350
I'll leave it to you, your generation,
to decide how you go about it.

